                <pb facs="0713" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363/398: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Piles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-26T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26, 1928—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Department’s telegram No. 24, May 25, 1 p.m. Today I returned the memorandum
                    in person to the President. He stated that the Ministry of Industry contends
                    that the decree should not be suspended as a whole and wishes time to present a
                    report, [omission?] declaring the President now has and will consider carefully
                    on Monday and hopes to issue an order next Tuesday which will embody his
                    personal views.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Piles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
